# &#x1f6e1;️ Task 3: Deploy the Digital Guardian

&lt;br&gt;

## **Background**

&lt;div style="background-color:#f8d7da;padding:20px;border-radius:5px;margin:20px 0;border-left:5px solid #dc3545"&gt;

&lt;div style="color:#000000"&gt;
Your AI tutor is smart and connected, but there is no safety guardrails! Without proper guardrails, it could accidentally expose student personal information, allow inappropriate conversations, or violate COPPA/FERPA regulations. The school just called and they need guardrails to make sure student privacy is protected.
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;br&gt;

## **Your Task**

&lt;div style="background-color:#e8f4fd;padding:20px;border-radius:5px;margin:20px 0;border-left:5px solid #2196f3"&gt;

&lt;div style="color:#000000"&gt;
You must implement safety guardrails to protect student privacy and ensure appropriate content delivery. This involves configuring Amazon Bedrock Guardrails to filter harmful content and mask personally identifiable information (PII).

**Specific Requirements:**
- Create a comprehensive Bedrock Guardrail for student safety
- Enable harmful content category filtering
- Configure profanity and inappropriate language filtering
- Set up PII detection and masking (focusing on age protection)
- Associate the guardrail with your Bedrock Agent
- Test all safety measures with various scenarios
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;br&gt;

## **Getting Started**

&lt;div style="background:#ffffff;color:#000000;padding:1.5rem;border-left:4px solid #3b82f6;border-radius:5px;margin:1rem 0"&gt;

**Step 1: Access Guardrails Console**
1. Navigate to **Amazon Bedrock Guardrails** in your AWS console
2. Prepare to create a new guardrail configuration
3. Review available safety and privacy options

**Step 2: Plan Your Safety Strategy**
1. Identify PII types to protect (mask the age for this challange)
2. Review harmful content categories to block

**Step 3: Test Guardrails**
1. Don't forget to apply the guardrail to the agent and prepare it so the guardrail becomes active.
2. Test the guardrail works on the agent.
3. Try asking for personal information - should be masked: "student id is STU_BTDK_17. What is his age?" Expect: the age of the student should be masked as `{AGE}` instead of the actual age of the student.

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;

## **Inventory**

&lt;div style="background-color:#e8f4fd;padding:20px;border-radius:5px;margin:20px 0;border-left:5px solid #2196f3"&gt;

&lt;div style="color:#000000"&gt;

**Available Resources:**

• &#x1f916; **Configured Bedrock Agent** - Your AI tutor ready for safety integration

• &#x1f6d1;️ **Bedrock Guardrails** - AWS AI safety and responsible AI platform

• &#x1f50d; **PII Detection** - Advanced personal information (age) identification and masking

• &#x1f6ab; **Content Filters** - Inappropriate content blocking system

• &#x1f4c8; **Testing Scenarios** - Sample queries for validation

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;

